# The type of `nil`, and the only value it has.
#
# Laid out as a pointer-width scalar because that is what `nil` compiles to:
# `Exception#capture_backtrace` writes `if symbols != nil` against a
# `Pointer<Pointer<UInt8>>`, and the comparison is a plain pointer compare.
# `IsAssignable` (Sema/.../TypeCompat.cpp) knows Nil only through the node kind
# it claims here — never by name — and lets it into any slot laid out the same
# way, which is every `Pointer<T>`.
#
# `T?` (NilableType) is a different question entirely and is **not**
# implemented: it needs a sum-type model Volt does not have. It is refused with
# an explicit diagnostic rather than accepted without semantics.

@[Primitive( "ptr", 64 ), Literal( NilLiteral )]
struct Nil
  include Comparable
end
